From 28c23a0e04ef5e68d08f12a1de835478710ca607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:14:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 47/53] drama: drama_voice.py runs only a tensorfold-native
 that can voice encode, and an explicit encoder wins

--native and --reference exclude each other. Without either, the tensorfold-native on PATH is used only when its --help lists voice encode; an older build is refused, not run. The seam tests drive stand-in binaries with and without voice encode.
---
 tools/zig/drama_voice.py      | 26 ++++++---
 tools/zig/drama_voice_test.py | 99 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 87 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/zig/drama_voice.py b/tools/zig/drama_voice.py
